1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:00,959
What happens if you

2
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:02,090
stop eating?

3
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:03,310
One man lasted

4
00:00:03,310 --> 00:00:05,867
three hundred and eighty-two days.

5
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:06,680
But first...

6
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:07,550
bite a lemon.

7
00:00:07,550 --> 00:00:08,340
In your head.

8
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:09,267
Now.

9
00:00:09,322 --> 00:00:10,669
Your mouth just watered,

10
00:00:10,669 --> 00:00:11,100
right?

11
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:11,827
That's your body

12
00:00:11,827 --> 00:00:13,330
getting ready for food...

13
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:14,890
from a thought.

14
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:15,565
Now imagine

15
00:00:15,565 --> 00:00:17,700
the food never comes.

16
00:00:17,728 --> 00:00:18,348
He climbed the mountain

17
00:00:18,348 --> 00:00:19,758
for one thing:

18
00:00:19,758 --> 00:00:21,448
Pip's favourite chocolate,

19
00:00:21,508 --> 00:00:23,267
from the shop at the top.

20
00:00:23,294 --> 00:00:24,444
On the way down,

21
00:00:24,444 --> 00:00:25,654
a storm hit.

22
00:00:25,654 --> 00:00:26,054
He made it

23
00:00:26,054 --> 00:00:27,454
to an empty hut...

24
00:00:27,454 --> 00:00:28,714
and a fox made it

25
00:00:28,714 --> 00:00:30,054
to his food bag.

26
00:00:31,402 --> 00:00:33,022
All he had left...

27
00:00:33,330 --> 00:00:34,533
was a lemon.

28
00:00:34,582 --> 00:00:35,152
The radio says

29
00:00:35,152 --> 00:00:36,072
the storm could last

30
00:00:36,072 --> 00:00:37,212
a week.

31
00:00:37,212 --> 00:00:38,032
And Pip has

32
00:00:38,032 --> 00:00:39,442
one question:

33
00:00:39,442 --> 00:00:40,992
"Is my chocolate okay?"

34
00:00:41,390 --> 00:00:42,610
Hour four.

35
00:00:42,610 --> 00:00:43,967
His stomach growls.

36
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,530
It's not asking for food...

37
00:00:45,530 --> 00:00:46,620
it's cleaning.

38
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:47,780
Every couple of hours,

39
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:48,544
an empty stomach

40
00:00:48,544 --> 00:00:50,333
squeezes out the leftovers.

41
00:00:50,390 --> 00:00:51,571
With nothing in there...

42
00:00:51,571 --> 00:00:52,933
it echoes.

43
00:00:52,970 --> 00:00:54,150
Hour six.

44
00:00:54,150 --> 00:00:55,240
Lunchtime...

45
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:57,260
and here comes the hunger,

46
00:00:57,260 --> 00:00:58,680
right on time.

47
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:00,420
It's not a fuel gauge.

48
00:01:00,420 --> 00:01:01,740
It's an alarm clock:

49
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:02,780
your body learned

50
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:04,233
when you eat.

51
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:05,470
Ignore it...

52
00:01:05,784 --> 00:01:07,290
and it goes quiet.

53
00:01:07,610 --> 00:01:08,900
Until dinner.

54
00:01:08,934 --> 00:01:10,134
Make a fist.

55
00:01:10,314 --> 00:01:11,133
Squeeze.

56
00:01:11,174 --> 00:01:12,154
Your muscles keep sugar

57
00:01:12,154 --> 00:01:13,234
for themselves.

58
00:01:13,554 --> 00:01:14,674
Your brain gets its sugar

59
00:01:14,674 --> 00:01:16,094
from your liver...

60
00:01:16,094 --> 00:01:16,874
and the liver's stash

61
00:01:16,874 --> 00:01:19,254
lasts a day or two.

62
00:01:19,325 --> 00:01:20,705
Hour eighteen.

63
00:01:20,745 --> 00:01:22,385
The stash is running low,

64
00:01:22,405 --> 00:01:23,105
and he just lost

65
00:01:23,105 --> 00:01:24,225
an argument...

66
00:01:24,225 --> 00:01:25,205
with a fox.

67
00:01:25,910 --> 00:01:27,050
Day one.

68
00:01:27,050 --> 00:01:28,265
And this...

69
00:01:28,265 --> 00:01:29,950
is the easy part.

70
00:01:30,228 --> 00:01:31,078
Day two.

71
00:01:31,078 --> 00:01:32,958
The brain still needs sugar,

72
00:01:33,008 --> 00:01:34,678
so the body makes more...

73
00:01:34,678 --> 00:01:35,478
from protein.

74
00:01:36,058 --> 00:01:37,158
Remember your fist?

75
00:01:37,178 --> 00:01:37,578
It's borrowing

76
00:01:37,538 --> 00:01:38,918
from muscle.

77
00:01:39,326 --> 00:01:40,266
Day three:

78
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:41,576
the big switch.

79
00:01:41,836 --> 00:01:42,316
The liver starts

80
00:01:42,316 --> 00:01:43,036
turning fat

81
00:01:43,036 --> 00:01:44,976
into a new fuel...

82
00:01:44,976 --> 00:01:45,476
and the brain

83
00:01:45,476 --> 00:01:47,333
starts running on it.

84
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:48,180
Turns out,

85
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:49,923
your body packed a lunch:

86
00:01:49,923 --> 00:01:50,965
weeks of it,

87
00:01:50,965 --> 00:01:52,150
as fat.

88
00:01:52,150 --> 00:01:53,280
That chocolate bar?

89
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:54,039
About a tenth

90
00:01:54,039 --> 00:01:55,406
of one day.

91
00:01:55,550 --> 00:01:56,750
Breathe on your hand.

92
00:01:56,750 --> 00:01:57,530
Smell it.

93
00:01:57,530 --> 00:01:58,880
Nail polish remover?

94
00:01:58,880 --> 00:01:59,470
No?

95
00:01:59,470 --> 00:02:00,650
By day three...

96
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:02,304
his breath might.

97
00:02:02,594 --> 00:02:03,874
And the weirdest part?

98
00:02:03,874 --> 00:02:05,174
For a lot of people,

99
00:02:05,174 --> 00:02:05,594
the hunger...

100
00:02:05,594 --> 00:02:07,394
gets quieter.

101
00:02:07,690 --> 00:02:09,220
In 1944,

102
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:10,509
thirty-six volunteers

103
00:02:10,509 --> 00:02:11,550
in Minnesota

104
00:02:11,550 --> 00:02:12,978
ate half their usual food

105
00:02:12,978 --> 00:02:14,233
for six months,

106
00:02:14,278 --> 00:02:15,301
so doctors could learn

107
00:02:15,301 --> 00:02:17,500
to feed a starving Europe.

108
00:02:17,530 --> 00:02:18,241
Their minds

109
00:02:18,241 --> 00:02:19,764
changed most.

110
00:02:19,764 --> 00:02:20,549
They read cookbooks

111
00:02:20,549 --> 00:02:21,750
like novels,

112
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:23,570
daydreamed about food...

113
00:02:23,570 --> 00:02:24,425
and chewed gum

114
00:02:24,425 --> 00:02:25,852
by the pack.

115
00:02:25,890 --> 00:02:26,960
Day five.

116
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:27,360
He's read

117
00:02:27,277 --> 00:02:28,380
the chocolate wrapper

118
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:29,916
eleven times.

119
00:02:29,916 --> 00:02:30,988
Now he reads it...

120
00:02:30,988 --> 00:02:32,467
to the fox.

121
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:32,900
Pip,

122
00:02:32,834 --> 00:02:33,883
on the radio:

123
00:02:33,883 --> 00:02:35,660
"Is my chocolate okay?"

124
00:02:35,737 --> 00:02:36,307
So how long

125
00:02:36,307 --> 00:02:37,560
could he last?

126
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:38,220
Nobody's allowed

127
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:39,230
to find out.

128
00:02:39,230 --> 00:02:40,367
Here's why.

129
00:02:40,408 --> 00:02:41,568
Find your pulse,

130
00:02:41,568 --> 00:02:43,468
on your neck or wrist.

131
00:02:43,468 --> 00:02:43,908
Count the beats

132
00:02:43,908 --> 00:02:45,528
for six seconds...

133
00:02:45,528 --> 00:02:46,408
go.

134
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:53,090
Add a zero.

135
00:02:53,090 --> 00:02:54,140
That's your heart rate:

136
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:54,903
most people get

137
00:02:54,903 --> 00:02:56,533
sixty to a hundred.

138
00:02:56,584 --> 00:02:57,454
The Minnesota men,

139
00:02:57,454 --> 00:02:58,534
by the end?

140
00:02:58,534 --> 00:02:59,874
About thirty-seven.

141
00:02:59,874 --> 00:03:01,494
A heart is a muscle...

142
00:03:01,494 --> 00:03:02,514
and a starving body

143
00:03:02,514 --> 00:03:04,294
eats muscle.

144
00:03:04,610 --> 00:03:05,500
With water,

145
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:06,402
most healthy people

146
00:03:06,402 --> 00:03:07,170
would last

147
00:03:07,170 --> 00:03:08,500
one to two months.

148
00:03:08,530 --> 00:03:09,990
After the fat runs out,

149
00:03:09,990 --> 00:03:10,730
the body eats

150
00:03:10,730 --> 00:03:12,211
its own protein...

151
00:03:12,211 --> 00:03:13,221
and in the end,

152
00:03:13,221 --> 00:03:14,296
the heart.

153
00:03:14,406 --> 00:03:15,816
Except one man.

154
00:03:15,816 --> 00:03:17,156
In 1965,

155
00:03:17,326 --> 00:03:18,016
Angus Barbieri

156
00:03:18,016 --> 00:03:18,916
weighed over

157
00:03:18,916 --> 00:03:20,976
two hundred kilos.

158
00:03:21,216 --> 00:03:22,656
With doctors watching,

159
00:03:22,656 --> 00:03:23,156
he lived on

160
00:03:23,156 --> 00:03:24,896
water and vitamins...

161
00:03:24,896 --> 00:03:25,656
for three hundred

162
00:03:25,656 --> 00:03:27,536
and eighty-two days.

163
00:03:27,856 --> 00:03:28,256
He lost

164
00:03:28,196 --> 00:03:31,256
a hundred and twenty-five kilos.

165
00:03:31,316 --> 00:03:32,366
And by the end,

166
00:03:32,366 --> 00:03:33,736
he went to the toilet...

167
00:03:33,736 --> 00:03:34,256
about once

168
00:03:34,256 --> 00:03:36,376
every forty days.

169
00:03:36,911 --> 00:03:37,787
His first meal,

170
00:03:37,787 --> 00:03:38,950
the papers said?

171
00:03:38,950 --> 00:03:40,760
One boiled egg.

172
00:03:41,062 --> 00:03:42,112
Day six.

173
00:03:42,632 --> 00:03:43,512
Midnight.

174
00:03:43,852 --> 00:03:45,592
The worst of the storm.

175
00:03:46,662 --> 00:03:47,152
He unwraps

176
00:03:47,152 --> 00:03:48,592
the chocolate...

177
00:03:50,430 --> 00:03:50,971
...and wraps it

178
00:03:50,971 --> 00:03:52,150
back up.

179
00:03:52,947 --> 00:03:53,877
Day seven.

180
00:03:53,877 --> 00:03:55,157
The storm breaks.

181
00:03:56,593 --> 00:03:57,276
The rescuers

182
00:03:57,276 --> 00:03:57,676
hand him

183
00:03:57,538 --> 00:03:58,700
a cup of soup.

184
00:03:58,700 --> 00:03:59,185
Your mouth

185
00:03:59,185 --> 00:04:00,480
just watered again,

186
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:01,130
didn't it?

187
00:04:01,130 --> 00:04:02,367
So did his.

188
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:03,330
Just a cup:

189
00:04:03,330 --> 00:04:03,790
after days

190
00:04:03,790 --> 00:04:05,070
without food,

191
00:04:05,070 --> 00:04:05,730
the first meals

192
00:04:05,730 --> 00:04:07,370
start small.

193
00:04:07,834 --> 00:04:08,654
At home,

194
00:04:08,654 --> 00:04:09,154
he hands Pip

195
00:04:09,154 --> 00:04:10,174
her chocolate.

196
00:04:10,174 --> 00:04:10,974
Not one bite

197
00:04:10,974 --> 00:04:11,894
missing.

198
00:04:12,470 --> 00:04:13,120
Every night,

199
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:13,612
she'd asked

200
00:04:13,612 --> 00:04:15,030
about the chocolate.

201
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:15,650
Because if

202
00:04:15,492 --> 00:04:17,440
the chocolate was okay...

203
00:04:17,812 --> 00:04:18,767
so was he.

204
00:04:20,750 --> 00:04:21,277
She gives him

205
00:04:21,277 --> 00:04:22,467
the bigger half.

206
00:04:24,587 --> 00:04:25,607
Next week:

207
00:04:25,607 --> 00:04:26,427
what happens if you

208
00:04:26,427 --> 00:04:28,687
stop brushing your teeth.

209
00:04:29,047 --> 00:04:29,647
Subscribe...

210
00:04:29,647 --> 00:04:30,947
and go eat something.

